# Excluded wholesale -- samples, audits and review sheets the runtime never reads -- except the
# built vocabulary the controlled kind and llm_run.py read (atrium-keyword-extract#1, #2): the
# nested vocabulary and its provenance sidecar (VOCAB_PATH), the two flat files beside it that
# resolve entities[].pid, and the taxonomy VocabularyManager reads to decide which themes reach
# the prompt and which geographic guardrail it must agree with. Without them an image's
# llm_config.txt names files the image does not carry, and the controlled kind cannot start.
data_samples/
!data_samples/taxonomy_config.json
!data_samples/taxonomy_overrides.json
!data_samples/vocab/union_nested.json
!data_samples/vocab/union_nested.meta.json
!data_samples/vocab/amcr_flat.json
!data_samples/vocab/teater_flat.json
# Not runtime (atrium-project#69, roadmap H5): ker_data/ holds two IDF pickles (26 MB) that
# no shipped code reads; the test suite runs on the CI runner; the dev logs are
# documentation.
ker_data/
tests/
agent_dev_logs/
# Vocabulary review tools, run from a checkout (README: the review sheets), never from an
# image: no published target's entrypoint (keywords.py, llm_run.py, service/api.py,
# openrouter_client.py, ollama_client.py) reaches them (atrium-project#72, "research off the
# release line"; .github/production-image.json is the api image's closure).
corpus_review.py
vocab_review.py
TEMP/
*.log
*.png
*.html
.cache/
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx
.env
